<title>FRANCE: Eiffage suspended limit-down.</title>
<headline>Eiffage suspended limit-down.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in public works group Eiffage was suspended, limit-down, on Monday morning after the company reported a first-half net attributable loss of 890 million francs, the French stockmarkets association SBF said.</p>
<p>Eiffage forecast a similar loss for the full year and suspended its 1996 dividend.</p>
<p>Trade in the stock set to resume at 0830 GMT, the SBF said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
